messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 506 and 249? Please reason step by step.. I think the correct answer is: 125894\n', "<think>.\nTo find the product of 506 and 249, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's a step-by-step breakdown:.\n\n1. Write down the numbers one below the other, aligning them by their place values:.\n   ```.\n     506.\n   x 249.\n   ------.\n   ```.\n\n2. Multiply 506 by the ones digit of 249 (which is 9):.\n   ```.\n     506.\n   x   9.\n   ------.\n     4554.\n   ```.\n\n3. Multiply 506 by the tens digit of 249 (which is 4), but remember to shift the result one position to the left because we're dealing with tens:.\n   ```.\n     506.\n   x  40.\n   ------.\n    20240.\n   ```.\n\n4. Multiply 506 by the hundreds digit of 249 (which is 2), and shift the result two positions to the left:.\n   ```.\n     506.\n   x 200.\n   ------.\n   101200.\n   ```.\n\n5. Add all the partial products together:.\n   ```.\n     4554.\n   +20240.\n   +101200.\n   -------.\n   126404.\n   ```.\n\nSo, the product of 506 and 249 is 126,404.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
